WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.402
-Charlize, you've been in
some giant, giant movies,

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:05.471
you've won an Oscar,

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:09.709
but the "F9" --
these "Fast and Furious" movies,

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.110
it's massive.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.647
The audiences, the fans
are just so passionate.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.382
When did you realize,
like, "Oh, this is --

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:19.552
I'm stepping into
a whole universe here."

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:22.287
-Yeah, I mean, listen,
I -- I'm not --

00:00:22.287 --> 00:00:24.657
It's hard not to know

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:28.127
just how impressive
these movies are,

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:31.764
and it's -- it's -- to step into
it is intimidating already,

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.533
just because of what
they've built

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.601
and have kind of nurtured
over the years.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:38.004
And people love these movies,

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:41.241
and they love
these characters deeply,

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:44.744
and the whole theme of family
runs so deep

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.679
in this franchise.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:51.818
So, when I when I showed up
as the baddie in "Fast 8",

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:56.356
and kind of like,
you know, turned Dom,

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.691
Vin Diesel's character,
against his family

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.927
in that -- in that movie,

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:03.696
I definitely had
a couple of fans --

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:06.366
It was like this -- like,
they appreciate a good villain,

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.466
but at the same time
they were like,

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:10.369
"How dare you do that to Dom?!

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:12.271
How dare you turn him against
the family?!"

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:13.406
And so it's like --
-Yeah, you don't mess with

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.874
the family!

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.076
-Yeah. It's always, like,
"But great job.

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:18.811
We want a good baddie.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.212
But don't do that again."

00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:23.349
I'm like, "Alright,
I won't mess with the family."

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.653
-And now you have to -- you have
to intimidate John Cena

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:29.021
in this movie,
who is a pal of ours,

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:32.825
and he's -- he's Dom's brother
in this movie.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:35.128
What's it like
working with Cena?

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:39.365
-Oh, my God,
he's just so incredible.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:42.101
I could not have asked
for a better scene partner.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:44.269
-He's funny, too.
-I was pretty exhausted

00:01:44.269 --> 00:01:46.205
coming off "Old Guard" --

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:47.907
like, it was two days after
that shoot,

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.408
which was a pretty long shoot.

00:01:49.408 --> 00:01:52.212
I was pretty bruised up.

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:54.146
I was just, like --
And then I was, like,

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:56.248
put in this box
and I had all this dialogue,

00:01:56.248 --> 00:01:57.684
and I definitely had
a couple of moments

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:59.218
where I was struggling
with my lines,

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:02.255
and this guy was just so, like,
right there.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:04.991
At some point -- At one point,
he, like, knew the line

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:07.293
that I missed and I was like,
"This guy, like,

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.228
he even, like, knows
the line that I just missed."

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.597
Like, just there supporting.
-He's a pro!

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:13.866
-He's funny and --
Yeah, and he's great.

00:02:13.866 --> 00:02:17.270
In the film,
he plays Dom's brother

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.638
and they have a lot of kind of,
like, unfinished business,

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:21.140
which is --
which is pretty cool.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.976
-Yeah. I want to show everyone
a clip from the movie.

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:27.747
Here's Charlize Theron
in "F9". Take a look at this.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:32.585
-East L.A. is a tough
enough place to grow up...

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:37.557
but it was your brother's shadow
that turned you into this,

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.125
isn't it?

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:41.293 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:45.565
So your whole life, you pushed
yourself to be faster than Dom,

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:52.237
smarter than Dom,
stronger than Dom.

00:02:52.237 --> 00:02:57.243
Tell me, do you hate him enough
that it keeps you up at night?

00:02:57.243 --> 00:03:00.113 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.714
Still?

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.715
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:05.885
-Who is better than
Charlize Theron?

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:07.086
Charlize Theron,
everybody.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:10.557
"F9" is in theaters today.
Check it out.

